# Test output. Added with the reporters that write it, in the same commit --
# an untracked reports/ directory appearing in someone else's working tree
# after their first test run is a change to their workflow nobody asked for.
#
# 🔴 LEADING SLASH, and it matters far more than it looks. A bare `reports` matches a
# directory of that name AT ANY DEPTH, so it also matched src/pages/reports/ -- and
# Tailwind v4's automatic source detection SKIPS whatever .gitignore matches. Every
# tracked file under src/pages/reports/ went unscanned, every utility class unique to
# those files was absent from the built CSS, and OrganizerReport's section headings
# rendered white on white: invisible. Found 2026-09-09 by the design arc's contrast
# gate; register row A42.
#
# `git check-ignore <path>` says NOTHING for a TRACKED file, which is why this hid so
# long -- the obvious command answers "not ignored". --no-index is the load-bearing
# half. THE GUARD IS src/test/ignoredSources.test.js: it runs in `npm test` and goes
# red if any tracked source file is shadowed again.
#
# The anchored form still ignores the test output at the repo root, which is all this
# rule was ever for.
/reports
/coverage
